  three, [38;5;153mlogin[39m becomes [1masync[0m and gains [1mno [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter[0m — it returns the server's [38;5;153muserId[39m. That's the inversion you
  already agreed to; the one call site at [38;5;153mapp.js:23[39m has to [38;5;153mawait[39m.

  - [1mMemoized readiness promise[0m — [38;5;153mauth.js[39m exposes [38;5;153mAuth.getUser()[39m, which returns a promise resolving to [38;5;153m{userId, username}
[39m    or [38;5;153mnull[39m. The first call fires [38;5;153m/me[39m; every later caller on that page gets the same in-flight promise, so N forms cost
